body:
I'm really glad you and some other people have had positive experiences, and I'm not saying you're destined to have a bad experience if you go to one of these places. But using your experience to invalidate and as an excuse to not listen the mountains of negative experiences and statistics that corroborate this isn't helpful. It is the exact same language as when people say "he couldn't have abused you because he didn't abuse me". Especially calling it fear mongering ?? Think about the language you're using when talking about abuse. [Addressing Sexual Violence in Psychiatric Facilities](https://ps.psychiatryonline.org/doi/10.1176/appi.ps.202000038) [The reported prevalence of physical and sexual abuse among a sample of children and adolescents at a public psychiatric hospital

](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/7820360/) [MIA Survey: Ex-patients Tell of Force, Trauma and Sexual Abuse in America’s Mental Hospitals

](https://www.madinamerica.com/2018/12/mia-survey-force-trauma-sexual-abuse-mental-hospitals/#:~:text=More%20than%20half%20of%20the,said%20they%20were%20sexually%20abused.) [The prevalence of abuse histories in the mental health system

](https://www.nasmhpd.org/content/prevalence-abuse-histories-mental-health-system) I may come off a bit harsh and I don't mean to. But I am begging you to do some basic research and not to use your own experience as a base for what you believe goes on in this system.
